    output slabs (89121c4), readback draining on partial batch failure
    (e59baef), and the two bit-exact cfx batch entries with per-block
    failure masks (bb463bf heights / 024c124 biomes); 2ec8385 adds the
    process-global batch metrics (counters, histograms, host walls) with
    the CUBIOMES_GPU_PROFILING=1 event-timer opt-in and its marker-canary
    capability probe; 6cdd027 adds the bit-exact fp64 sparse-point kernels
    and entries (gpuCfxOverviewHeightsSparse / gpuCfxSurfaceBiomesSparse)
    that serve one refinement chunk in a single kernel launch and readback
    with whole-or-nothing rejection, make FP_CONTRACT OFF actually reach
    both built programs, and pin the per-chunk launch/read counts in the
    metrics harness; d70551e adds the fp32 sparse twins
    (gpuCfxOverviewHeightsSparseFloat / gpuCfxSurfaceBiomesSparseFloat):
    the same cfx kernel source compiled a second time in single precision
    (cfx_real typedef + -cl-single-precision-constant) against float
    mirrors of the packed tables, drift-budgeted instead of bit-exact -
    the typedef refactor leaves the fp64 build byte-equivalent (the exact
    matrix reproduces identically) and the rect/float-family kernels are
    untouched. 14c2eb3 adds the surface-columns point kernels for the mod's
    exact-columns stage (gpuCfxSurfaceColumnsPoints plus the drift-budgeted
    float twin gpuCfxSurfaceColumnsPointsFloat): n anchors solved in one
    launch and readback with the four output planes carrying the CPU's own
    fluid post-pass and INT32_MIN sentinel, whole-or-nothing rejection as on
